# BuildKit reads `<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore` (this file) in preference to a
# context-root .dockerignore, so the ignore stays scoped to server/Dockerfile
# even though the build context is the PACK ROOT. Paths are relative to that
# context root. Whitelist style: ignore everything, then re-include only the
# trees the Dockerfile COPYs (keeps the context tiny and node_modules out).
*

# Re-include exactly what the Dockerfile needs.
!server/package.json
!server/package-lock.json
!server/tsconfig.json
!server/src
!contracts/src
!content/topologies

# Never ship installed deps or build junk even if re-included by a parent rule.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.DS_Store
